{"card_hash": "c26cebd4504e3d00659bd3c5dd2210c066241c6fe48a0ba376dd8159a9cfd34c", "channel": "Dwarkesh Patel", "chars": 75184, "chars_all_clips": 75184, "chars_chosen_clips": 1200, "clip_count": 85, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=101", "end": 204.16, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "899084656dd7b173c80c0f0c81e350300a727883b755415c357093e0e64c243f", "start": 101.36, "text": "Up until now, they have been companies that mostly lost money. Anthropic started turning a profit in Q2. It’s believed at some point in Q3, OpenAI could start turning a profit even, with the bigger rise of Codex and 5.6 and all this. But if", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=1715", "end": 1781.52, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "600725843ef820b68d1ccef9cdffc4c617764b4142088949961f21c1872cbccf", "start": 1715.76, "text": "Obviously, who captures the value is still up for debate, but ultimately everyone’s going to raise their prices. Because they can, and it’s super inflationary. Especially if the method of regulation is… Right now, so far, it’s just \"don’t r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2670", "end": 2746.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "09638001dc44956b1f7e2ac830ce1bfe9c77264c8fc09d5ee9de90ace3196b9e", "start": 2670.32, "text": "But still, at the current size of the US economy, it’ll be like a third to a quarter of the US economy just going towards data centers. As I say that out loud, I’m like, \"Maybe you’re right and we just won’t allow it, and that’s the reason ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2987", "end": 3051.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "cbb238a78236082f535a96a1ff64b80c43eca3b3f2a334bb0696442d7da2dfdc", "start": 2987.44, "text": "They’re competing against the other lending that the government would’ve done, or that other companies would’ve done, or that you as a consumer or a mortgage buyer would’ve done. That’s making it more expensive for everybody else to borrow.", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=4032", "end": 4131.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "a7e63ef51d0fc21cb04c2847059f8a1d66a1eb759eb1a22eec78272851d89729", "start": 4032.08, "text": "The Jane Street team follows frontier LLM research closely. A relatively common intern project is adapting a recent paper to financial markets, which come with their own set of gnarly problems. Ultimately, we're trying to model thousands of", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=101", "end": 204.16, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "899084656dd7b173c80c0f0c81e350300a727883b755415c357093e0e64c243f", "start": 101.36, "text": "Up until now, they have been companies that mostly lost money. Anthropic started turning a profit in Q2. It’s believed at some point in Q3, OpenAI could start turning a profit even, with the bigger rise of Codex and 5.6 and all this. But if", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=1715", "end": 1781.52, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "600725843ef820b68d1ccef9cdffc4c617764b4142088949961f21c1872cbccf", "start": 1715.76, "text": "Obviously, who captures the value is still up for debate, but ultimately everyone’s going to raise their prices. Because they can, and it’s super inflationary. Especially if the method of regulation is… Right now, so far, it’s just \"don’t r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2670", "end": 2746.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "09638001dc44956b1f7e2ac830ce1bfe9c77264c8fc09d5ee9de90ace3196b9e", "start": 2670.32, "text": "But still, at the current size of the US economy, it’ll be like a third to a quarter of the US economy just going towards data centers. As I say that out loud, I’m like, \"Maybe you’re right and we just won’t allow it, and that’s the reason ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2987", "end": 3051.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "cbb238a78236082f535a96a1ff64b80c43eca3b3f2a334bb0696442d7da2dfdc", "start": 2987.44, "text": "They’re competing against the other lending that the government would’ve done, or that other companies would’ve done, or that you as a consumer or a mortgage buyer would’ve done. That’s making it more expensive for everybody else to borrow.", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=4032", "end": 4131.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "a7e63ef51d0fc21cb04c2847059f8a1d66a1eb759eb1a22eec78272851d89729", "start": 4032.08, "text": "The Jane Street team follows frontier LLM research closely. A relatively common intern project is adapting a recent paper to financial markets, which come with their own set of gnarly problems. Ultimately, we're trying to model thousands of", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320", "end": null, "evidence_kind": "text_only", "excerpt_id": "2c8b1b855f151cd4954f59979b875b6cabc833ca082459755ab477d3bac4ec03", "start": null, "text": "\u003c!-- HOOK_START --\u003e \u003c!-- HOOK_END --\u003e Had a lot of fun chatting again with my twin brother @dylan522p   We went through lab economics over the next few years - the shift from inference to training as RSI draws near; and how Anthropic and Op", "timing": "not_timed", "truncated": true}], "hint": null, "platform": "x", "profile": "librarian", "schema_version": 1, "selection_version": "spread-longest-v2", "slug": "Dwarkesh_Patel_-_Had_a_lot_of_fun_chatting_again_with_my_twin_brother_dylan522p", "source_revision": "dc460f17e10a06ba3c59911355cfbc299440fe0be37e7720c9991b1feae4b123", "source_type": "x_thread", "status": "evidenced", "summary_hint": null, "title": "Dwarkesh Patel - Had a lot of fun chatting again with my twin brother @dylan522p   We ...", "topic": "AI and ML", "truncated": true, "truncation": {"byte_budget": true, "fields": ["hint"], "selection": true}, "url": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320", "video_id": "2092270658524745728", "yoinked_at": "2026-08-25T18:14:05"}
